This is a CPU-reviewed proposal for a NEW unmeasured collector only, NOT an
applicable patch to frozen v2. tensor_metadata/make_cast_observer come from
proposed_binding_probe.py. An independently authorized future collector would
create one observer before capture and put the UNCHANGED capture_body inside
its context. Observe-only records weak references; the retention-control arm
stores the very same real aten._to_copy results through replay/reset/sync.
Both arms must use the same observer API and original adapter/positions/math;
no kernel substitution, registration, source edit, timing or tolerance change.
Persist snapshots BEFORE any accuracy assertion. Expose retained outputs only
after real replay/sync for full original int32 positions comparison, never read
dead-process pointers or claim Python wrapper absence proves freed graph storage.
This patch alone cannot recover native packed QK argument values from pArguments.
